The phone scanner (the phone page at /scanner, src/web/scanner, and the connection code it
shares with the app, src/web/src/lib/scan_link.js) connects a phone to the computer over WebRTC
with Trystero, which passes the connection's set-up messages through Nostr relays. Trystero
(the trystero, @trystero-p2p/nostr and @trystero-p2p/core packages) and the Schnorr signing
library it signs Nostr events with are bundled into the page's inlined script. Both are used
under the MIT licence, which is compatible with the Apache License 2.0. Their exact versions are
pinned in src/web/package.json and src/web/deno.lock.

