The page's Tools > Rough scan draws the QR code a phone scans with uqr, a QR code encoder
bundled into the page's inlined script, itself a port of Project Nayuki's QR Code generator.
It is used under the MIT licence, which is compatible with the Apache License 2.0. Its exact
version is pinned in src/web/package.json and src/web/deno.lock. The web tests decode the
codes with jsQR (cozmo/jsQR, Apache License 2.0), a test-only dependency that does not ship in
the page.

